name: Emblem
description: Icons with default images and emblems (icon module)
version: @VERSION@
date: @DATE@
author: Björn Hagström
submitter: Björn Hagström
email:
url:
category: utility/workbench
replaces:
requirements: AmigaOS 4.1 (icon.library 51.15+), z.library 53
license: Public domain
minosversion: 4.1
texttype: Plain text
distribute: yes
hend:

Emblem lets an icon borrow a shared default image (a drawer, a page) and
put an emblem on it: a small picture that says what is inside, like a
note for music or a globe for internet things. The emblem can get a soft
shadow or a glow, or be grayed, darkened or brightened.

It is an icon module for icon.library (LIBS:IconModules), so Workbench,
file managers and every other program that shows icons show the result.
Change one image in ENVARC:sys/emblem and every icon that uses it
changes with it. No patches.

Four tool types do it:

  IMAGE=DrawerNS
  IMAGESELECTED=DrawerS
  EMBLEM=EmblemMusic,28,28,34,32,SHADOW
  EMBLEMSELECTED=EmblemMusic,28,28,34,32,SHADOW

Features:

- Default images and emblems as PNG files (any PNG; true colour with
  alpha is best), scaled to the size the tool type asks for.
- Effects per layer: SHADOW, GLOW, GRAY, DARK, BRIGHT, NONE; a settings
  file chooses the effect for tool types without one, and the shadow and
  glow look (offset, softness, opacity, colour).
- INTERNAL: an icon's own picture as the emblem (a program's picture on
  a drawer image).
- The icon's own pictures are always kept: saving never stores the
  composed picture, and converting back gives the original icon.
- New or changed images show on the next icon load, without a restart.
- Icons need the module's own file format; the EmblemIcon command
  converts icons to it and back, one by one, by pattern, or whole drawer
  trees.
- Sample art (placeholder, public domain), ten example icons, an
  AmigaGuide manual, and an Install script that installs, updates and
  removes everything (removing turns Emblem icons back into normal ones).

After installing, restart the computer: icon.library loads icon modules
only when it starts.

Based on openamiga.org project 34 "Emblem icon plugin" (2008), written
anew.

History:

- 1.0 (15.11.2026): first release.
